From 51cf2fcd68f343d3731ba4d4a16567ebdfc6cecb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola <francesco-stimola@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:19:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] vl/compositor: render the V plane with its own gfx
 shaders

The graphics path renders both chroma planes of a three-plane target,
such as I420 or YV12, with the UV shaders. They write U and V to the
first two channels, so the single-channel V plane gets U, and VA video
processing to these formats turns pictures green and magenta. The
compute path already has separate U and V shaders.

Add V variants of the YUV deinterlace and RGB-to-YUV fragment shaders,
writing V to the first channel, and use them for the V plane.

Tested on a GeForce GT 240M with ffmpeg's scale_vaapi converting to
yuv420p: decoded H.264 now matches software decoding on all three
planes, where the V plane was at 7 dB PSNR before. Converting RGB
frames, the V plane went from 6.9 to 24.5 dB, level with the U plane.
